"type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"font names. The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vs. a music font.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLFont","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfont","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDefaults":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldefaults","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The defaults type specifies score-wide defaults for scaling; whether or not the file is a concert score;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"layout; and default values for the music font, word font, lyric font, and lyric language. Except for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"concert-score element, if any defaults are missing, the choice of what to use is determined by the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"application."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLDefaults","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLDefaults","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDefaults","title":"MXLDefaults"},"doc